# Plan: Bristle Brushwerks False-Positive Cleanup

> **Status:** COMPLETE (2026-10-19)  
> **Date:** 2026-10-19  
> **Category:** bugs  
> **Investigation:** matched brush data 2020-01 → present (~1,399 “bristle” mentions)
>
> **Session notes:** User approved plan + YAML + fiber_utils in this pass; added Brothers
> Bristle handle entry themselves. Tightened `handles.yaml` / `knots.yaml` /
> `handles_new_structure.yaml` to `bristle.*brush ?w[eo]rks?`. Extended
> `fiber_utils` Boar with qualified bristle phrases. Added Bruskwerks typo to
> correct_matches. Rematch of FP months → 0 BBW false positives; 110 true BBW
> still present in sample. Brothers Bristle now splits to handle=Brothers Bristle
> + knot=AP Shave Co/Tuxedo.

**Goal:** Stop fiber-language “bristle … brush” strings from matching as Bristle Brushwerks (handle/knot), keep real BBW matches, and leave a regression net so this does not come back.

**Architecture:** Root cause is catalog regex overreach in `handles.yaml` / `knots.yaml` (and the unused twin in `handles_new_structure.yaml`). Align those patterns with the safer `brushes.yaml` pattern, add unit regression tests for the FP corpus, fix leftover edge strings via `correct_matches` where needed, then rematch a sample of months to confirm.

**Tech stack:** YAML catalogs, pytest matcher tests, `python run.py match --force`

**Spec:** Findings from 2026-10-19 investigation (this plan embeds them).

---

## Problem summary

| Signal | Count (2020+) |
|--------|----------------|
| Clear BBW (Brushwerks/Brushworks/Werks in text) | ~645 mentions / ~84 unique — matched correctly |
| Fiber / other “bristle” | ~731 mentions / ~116 unique — mostly correct |
| **False positives** (matched BBW, no brand name) | **22 mentions / 12 unique** |

**Nobody writes bare “Bristle” for the maker.** Brand hits always include Brushwerks / Brush Werks / Brushworks / Brush Works (rarely Bruskwerks). Fiber hits use boar / pure / bleached / unbleached / Zenith “XL/Bristle”.

### Root cause

```yaml
# handles.yaml + knots.yaml (BAD)
- ^(?!.*horse bristle).*bristle.*brush

# brushes.yaml (GOOD)
- bristle.*brush ?w[eo]rks?
```

The bad pattern matches any string containing “bristle” then later “brush” (except “horse bristle”), so Omega/Semogue/Zenith fiber phrases become BBW handles/knots.

`fiber_utils.py` does **not** map bare “bristle” → Boar (only `bristle & badger` / `badger & bristle` → Mixed). No change required there for this bug; optional follow-up below.

